  "seoBody": "<h2>Can I use Jotform for inspection reports?</h2><p>You can collect inspection data with Jotform, and it does that very well. What you get is a submission: rows, or a PDF laid out as the form. That is often enough for an internal record. It is a problem when a client or regulator expects a report. Turning submissions into a report is a desk job that is on no price list.</p><h2>How much does Jotform cost?</h2><p>The Starter plan is free, with 5 forms and 100 submissions a month. Paid plans are Bronze at $39, Silver at $49 and Gold at $129 a month. Paid tiers are single-user. On sticker price Jotform is cheaper than Quickler.</p><h2>What does Quickler do that a form builder does not?</h2><p>It writes the report. You answer in WhatsApp or Telegram by text, voice note, photo, document or location pin. When you say done, Quickler writes everything into your own report. Faults are listed by place, and each becomes a job.</p><h2>When should I just use Jotform?</h2><p>When you need data, not a finished document. If the answers feed a spreadsheet and nobody formats a report, a form builder is the right and cheaper tool.</p>",
